OpenSubs for the Mac App Store
==============================

OpenSubs is free software under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 or later (LICENSE, beside this file). Its source is at
https://github.com/open-subs/opensubs. This copy of the app was built from
that source by apps/desktop/scripts/build-appstore.sh.

It carries the following parts, each under its own licence. Their licence
texts are in the folders named.

ffmpeg and ffprobe (Contents/Resources/vendor/)
  FFmpeg 7.1.1, built from source by apps/desktop/scripts/ffmpeg-lgpl.sh as
  an LGPL build: no component under the GPL and nothing nonfree. FFmpeg is
  licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.
  It is statically linked with:
    FreeType 2.13.3   FreeType License (FTL)
    FriBidi 1.0.16    GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later
    HarfBuzz 10.4.0   MIT ("Old MIT") licence
    libass 0.17.3     ISC licence
    dav1d 1.5.1       BSD 2-Clause licence
    zimg 3.0.5        WTFPL, version 2
  and with the system's own zlib, bzip2, iconv, libc++, VideoToolbox and
  AudioToolbox. The exact configure line is in licences/ffmpeg/BUILD.txt.
  The complete corresponding source of FFmpeg and of every library above,
  as the archives it was built from, is in licences/ffmpeg/source/. The
  licence texts are in licences/ffmpeg/.

  These two programs are separate from OpenSubs: the app runs them to read
  a video and to write the subtitled one, and you may replace them with any
  ffmpeg and ffprobe built from modified sources.

Speech recognition
  whisper.cpp (MIT licence), compiled into the app through the whisper-rs
  crate (Unlicense). The Whisper Base model (ggml-base.bin, Contents/
  Resources/models/) is OpenAI's Whisper, released under the MIT licence.

Translation on the Mac
  CTranslate2 (MIT licence), compiled into the app through the ct2rs crate
  (MIT), with SentencePiece (Apache-2.0). The translation model (Contents/
  Resources/models/m2m100/) is Meta's M2M-100 418M, released under the MIT
  licence, converted to CTranslate2's int8 format by the OpenSubs project.

The account and credits
  The account elements (@openapps/ui) and client (@openapps/sdk) are under
  MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option.

The app itself is a Tauri 2 application (MIT OR Apache-2.0); the Rust and
JavaScript libraries it is built from keep their own licences, listed in
the source repository's Cargo.lock and package-lock.json files.
